+/-- An improved upper bound $N / e^{\sqrt{\log N}/16}$. This is below $N/(\log N)^k$
+for every fixed $k$, so it sits beneath the whole polylogarithmic scale on which
+`bestUpper` lives. -/
+noncomputable def improvedUpper (N : ℕ) : ℝ :=
+  (N : ℝ) / Real.exp (Real.sqrt (Real.log N) / 16)
+
 /--
 For which values of $k$ is the following true: whenever we partition $[N] = A_1 \cup \dots \cup A_k$,
 $\left|\bigcup^k_{i=1} (A_i \hat{+} A_i)\right| \geq \frac{1}{10} N$?
@@ -117,4 +123,23 @@ theorem green_25.variants.upper_ess89_trivial :
     ¬ ∀ᶠ N in atTop, Property25 (k N) N := by
   sorry
 
+/--
+An explicit improvement on the [ESS89] upper bound: there is a partition size
+$k(N) = O(N / e^{\sqrt{\log N}/16})$ for which the property fails for every
+large $N$.
+
+This is below every polylogarithmic rate $N/(\log N)^k$, so in particular it is
+$o(N/\log N) = o(\texttt{bestUpper})$. Stating the rate directly, rather than as
+`=o[atTop] bestUpper`, names the bound that the construction achieves. Note that
+the conclusion here is `∀ᶠ N, ¬ Property25 …`, which is stronger than the
+`¬ ∀ᶠ N, Property25 …` appearing in `green_25.upper`.
+-/
+@[category research solved, AMS 5 11]
+theorem green_25.variants.upper_exp_sqrt_log :
+    ∃ k : ℕ → ℕ,
+      (∀ᶠ N in atTop, 1 ≤ k N ∧ k N ≤ N) ∧
+      (fun N => (k N : ℝ)) =O[atTop] improvedUpper ∧
+      ∀ᶠ N in atTop, ¬ Property25 (k N) N := by
+  sorry
+
 end Green25
